# 1-based lines to bookmark. Each sits INSIDE a construct the profile claims to
# understand, so a broken `containers` shows up as a missing breadcrumb.
#
# Lines are chosen to be structurally distinct from their siblings. Codemark
# refuses a bookmark whose generated query matches more than one node, so a
# statement with an identically-shaped sibling is not a usable anchor.

# The deepest chain: a hook callback inside a function component —
# InvoiceView > useMemo(() => ...) > for > if.
44

# A JSX element inside a `.map` callback inside the component's markup. Proves
# the TSX grammar parses JSX (the TypeScript grammar cannot) and that a
# self-closing element is reachable by tag name.
59

# A JSX element with children, pinned by its tag name inside the component.
64

# Inside an exported arrow-function component — the shape export_statement and
# lexical_declaration exist to anchor.
73

# Inside a for loop inside a class method: class InvoiceStore > markPaid.
94

# NOT bookmarkable, recorded rather than silently omitted:
#
#   51    setStatus(Status.Paid);
#
# Its sibling `onPay(total);` has the same shape, so the generated query
# matches both and codemark refuses it. Not a profile problem.
